{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01TC", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-quasi-finite-locally-quasi-compact}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:91f7f690005974538f9413d26e06567c7aaac53ad99387d497b14ae3e3c887e8", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9a34b12669d3bf93e1931aaeb58214359f7aa5990413bcdc13e124843f24a171", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nThen <MATH_0002> is quasi-finite if and only if <MATH_0003> is\nlocally quasi-finite and quasi-compact.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9fa406bc4de1d29acd925339e463d39ac70d9ba2c84cfc74854ffda496f6a622", "unit_id": "tag:01TJ:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01TC", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f$", "MATH_0002": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$x$", "MATH_0005": "$f$", "MATH_0006": "$f$", "MATH_0007": "$f$", "MATH_0008": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0009": "$x$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-finite-type}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-quasi-finite-at-point-characterize}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-quasi-finite-at-point-characterize}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1ddc15e012a19d1fd37a7392e05417f69a0428718cc86df17fcb01bd4b857af9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d0a8ba3f398af869f3cda993b9859c3ea6d5acf64ca032b4f36204f562229fc4", "source_text": "Assume <MATH_0001> is quasi-finite. It is quasi-compact by Definition\n<REF_0001>. Let <MATH_0002>.\nWe see that <MATH_0003> is quasi-finite at <MATH_0004> by\nLemma <REF_0002>.\nHence <MATH_0005> is quasi-compact and locally quasi-finite.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nAssume <MATH_0006> is quasi-compact and locally quasi-finite.\nThen <MATH_0007> is of finite type. Let <MATH_0008> be a point.\nBy Lemma <REF_0003>\nwe see that <MATH_0009> is an isolated point of its fibre.\nThe lemma is proved.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ec74b9d469cc3edb354f6f347f1bf60e0bf934b27417cdf26019f17ac15dd9e7", "unit_id": "tag:01TJ:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01TC", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-quasi-finite}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:91f7f690005974538f9413d26e06567c7aaac53ad99387d497b14ae3e3c887e8", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:978b98fd9e9e3ef327002bb93f8077be17c775035d7e2024062d3b803f4b20a0", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nThe following are equivalent:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0002> is quasi-finite, and\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0003> is locally of finite type, quasi-compact, and has finite fibres.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4b9994e73ad8628721ab029c6ddef42be82052265e1a908516c7929cdf27154e", "unit_id": "tag:02NH:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01TC", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$s \\in S$", "MATH_0004": "$x \\in X_s$", "MATH_0005": "$X_s$", "MATH_0006": "$X_s = \\bigcup_{x \\in X_s} \\{x\\}$", "MATH_0007": "$f$", "MATH_0008": "$X_s$", "MATH_0009": "$X_s$", "MATH_0010": "$f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-finite-fibre}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-quasi-finite-locally-quasi-compact}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7b274d01fd2b8f1c37087d20cf2be74c33fc00806c9225542aeae81785dd819e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d741381e39182c49413926818691cb459024ef0b027187d0af2a578e1cf81926", "source_text": "Assume <MATH_0001> is quasi-finite. In particular <MATH_0002> is locally of finite type\nand quasi-compact (since it is of finite type). Let <MATH_0003>. Since\nevery <MATH_0004> is isolated in <MATH_0005> we see that\n<MATH_0006> is an open covering. As <MATH_0007>\nis quasi-compact, the fibre <MATH_0008> is quasi-compact. Hence we see\nthat <MATH_0009> is finite.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nConversely, assume <MATH_0010> is locally of finite type, quasi-compact\nand has finite fibres. Then it is locally quasi-finite by\nLemma <REF_0001>. Hence it is quasi-finite by\nLemma <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d95b7c0e61dd4e1f7822d01df683d366f2ff36b76919f9bc4d24ecc851534392", "unit_id": "tag:02NH:proof"}
